The reason you received an error when you added isFinalApproval is a **method signature mismatch**. If you change the parameters of a method from (LocalDateTime) to (LocalDateTime, boolean), Java will immediately throw an error everywhere else in your code that is still trying to call it with just one parameter.
Here is the complete, updated method, along with the exact line you must fix inside your processWorkflowAction method to resolve the error.
### 1. Replace the validateScheduledTime method
Replace your existing method at the bottom of the file with this new version:
```java
    public void validateScheduledTime(LocalDateTime scheduledTime, boolean isFinalApproval) {
        if (scheduledTime == null) return;
        
        LocalDateTime now = LocalDateTime.now();
        LocalDateTime maxTime = now.with(java.time.LocalTime.MAX);

        if (isFinalApproval) {
            // Rule for Final Approvers: Just make sure it's not in the past
            if (scheduledTime.isBefore(now)) {
                throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Scheduled time cannot be in the past.");
            }
        } else {
            // Rule for Creators: Must be ~30 minutes in the future
            LocalDateTime minTime = now.plusMinutes(28); 
            if (scheduledTime.isBefore(minTime)) {
                throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Scheduled time must be at least 30 minutes from the current time.");
            }
        }

        if (scheduledTime.isAfter(maxTime)) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Scheduled time cannot exceed today's end of day (11:59 PM).");
        }
    }

```
### 2. Fix the caller in processWorkflowAction
If you look around **line 114** in the code you just shared, inside the if (isFinalStep) block, you have this code:
```java
            if (isOverride) {
                if (dto.getNewScheduledTime() != null) {
                    validateScheduledTime(dto.getNewScheduledTime()); // <-- THIS IS CAUSING THE ERROR
                }

```
Because this is happening during the Final Approval step, you must update that line to pass true to the new parameter.
**Change it to this:**
```java
            if (isOverride) {
                if (dto.getNewScheduledTime() != null) {
                    // Pass 'true' because this override is happening at Final Approval
                    validateScheduledTime(dto.getNewScheduledTime(), true); 
                }

```
